 "bio": "Sepp Hochreiter heads the Institute for Machine Learning at Johannes Kepler University Linz and is co-founder and chief scientist of NXAI. Hochreiter is a co-inventor of the Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) network and senior author of xLSTM, a recurrent architecture presented at NeurIPS 2024 as an alternative to transformers. NXAI builds on xLSTM, including the xLSTM 7B language model and the TiRex time-series model.",
